  "english": "23. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. First [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers (Harts): \"Blessed art thou, Lord\" (Orhneal es ter). Lord's Prayer/Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 8 [dk]: \"The choirs of angels\" (Hreshtakatsn dasq), and \"Thy Angel\" (Hreshtak qo).\n\n24. Monday. Tone 1 [ATS]. [Feast of] Julian and Vasilouhi. Canticle of the Fathers (Harts) Tone 4 [bk]: \"We bless thee, Lord\" (Orhnemq ezqez ter).\n\n30. Sunday. Tone 7 [DZ]. Second [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers (Harts) Tone 2 [ak]: \"Unoriginate Word\" (Anskizbn band). Lord's Prayer/Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 7 [dz]: \"Who art above\" (Or i verd es). See also the others in the First Volume.\n\nDecember\n\n1. Monday. Tone 8 [DK]. [Feast of] Gennarius and Mercurius, and of Jacob and Irava-P'har [Just-Glorious].\n\n2. Tuesday. Tone 1 [ATS]. [Feast of] Cornelius the Centurion, and of Simeon, and the others.\n\n7. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK]. Third [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers (Harts) Tone 5 [bz]: \"Who art the King\" (Or t'agavord es). Lord's Prayer/Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 6 [gk]: \"Taking and our\" (Areal ev mer). Fast-break (Barekendan) of the Fast of Saint James.\n\n9. Tuesday. Tone 8 [DK]. Fast. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n\n10. Wednesday. Tone 1 [ATS]. Fast. Canticle of the Fathers (Harts) Tone 8 [dk]: \"God of our fathers, have mercy\" (Astvats harts'n merots oghormya).\n\n14. Sunday. Tone 5 [GZ]. Fourth [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers (Harts) Tone 4 [bk]: \"Unoriginate God\" (Anskizbn astvats). Lord's Prayer/Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 5 [gz]: \"Glorified is thy resurrection\" (P'aravoryal e qo yarut'iund).\n\n21. Sunday. Tone 4 [BK]. Fifth [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers (Harts) Tone 5 [gz]: \"Glorified Son of God\" (P'aravoryal ordi astutso). Lord's Prayer/Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 4 [bk]: \"Christ is risen\" (K'ristos yarev), and \"Morning\" (Aravotyan), and \"They anticipated\" (Kankhets'in).\n\n22. Monday. Tone 5 [GZ]. [Feast of] Abraham and Khoren, Cosmas and Damian, and of Astvatsatur [Theodotos] the Martyr. Canticle of the Fathers (Harts) Tone 8 [dk]: \"To thee, God\" (Ar qez astvats).\n\n23. Tuesday. Tone 6 [GK]. [Feast of] David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n\n28. Sunday. Tone 3 [BZ]. Sixth [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers (Harts) Tone 6 [gk]: \"Before eternity\" (Nakhahavityan). Lord's Prayer/Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 3 [bz]: \"Today they rejoiced\" (Aysor zvart'ats'an).\n\n29. Monday. Tone 4 [BK]. [Feast of the] Sons of Thunder [James and John]. Fast-break (Barekendan) of the Nativity Fast.\n\n30. Tuesday. Tone 5 [GZ]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Canticle of the Fathers (Harts) Tone 6 [gk]: \"Blessed Lord God, blessed\" (Orhneal ter astvats orhneal). And see the others in order.\n\nJanuary\n\n4. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Seventh [Sunday of Advent]. Fast. Lord's Prayer/Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 2 [ak]: \"Wonderful is the Resurrection\" (Hrashali zyarut'iun).\n\n5. Monday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ.\n\nSeven-Day Cycle of the Romans:\n\n19. Saturday. [Feast of] Theodosius the Emperor, and the Children of Ephesus.\n\n20. Sunday. First [Sunday after Epiphany]. Canticle of the Fathers (Harts) Tone 5 [dz]: \"The dawning of the Only-Begotten\" (Tsagumn miatsni).\n\n21. Monday. [Feast of] Cyriacus and Julietta, and of Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Gregory.\n\n22. Tuesday. [Feast of] Vahan of Goghtn, and of Eugine the Virgin, and the others.\n\nJanuary\n\n6. SUNDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The meat-eating season (non-fasting period) is twenty-two days.\n\n14. Monday. [Feast of] John the Forerunner [Baptist].\n\n15. Tuesday. [Feast of] Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and the others.\n\n17. Thursday. [Feast of] Anton [Anthony] the Anchorite.",
